comments.body:
@shubhshah01 thank you, it would be great if you could send the log file. Can you share some information about the data movement? (i.e. how much data is being write to the collection)? This will help us replicate the issue and test it. 

We have also noticed that you are using Airbyte v0.57.2, we do recommend updating to the newest version (see our [Releases page](https://github.com/airbytehq/airbyte-platform/releases)). There is also a new version for the MongoDb source (see [chnagelogs](https://docs.airbyte.com/integrations/sources/mongodb-v2#changelog)). 
 Can you please upgrade to the latest versions and keep me posted if the error is recurring?

> [@ivan-sukhomlyn](https://github.com/ivan-sukhomlyn) try to increase `Size of the queue (Advanced)` in source config, may help this issue

@ivan-sukhomlyn, did you increase this value? Did it solve your problem? I'm also currently facing the same issue with MongoDB Atlas. I have a 7-day oplog window size and after 7 days the Airbyte sync starts failing with the same message (scheduled syncs every 6 hours and now every 3 hours).

@whanata, do you know if this fix you proposed is already being submitted as a pull request or if anyone on Airbyte's side is aware and working on the fix?

@raphaelsampaio no, it has **not** fixed that issue.

I've also upgraded the MongoDB source to the 2.x version in the hope that there will be some improvement here.

Sometimes we see situations where the **resume token depends on the UUID of the not-synced collection** in MongoDB. So, it could be a reason in case of partial sync of the DB to destination

@raphaelsampaio 
I didn't propose a fix, I propose the current workaround right now is I have to manually update the connection state.
I'm not sure if anyone from Airbyte is looking into this problem as of now.

@rodireich 
We’re experiencing the same issue.
Could we also get access to the build so we can test it on our side?

@rodireich thanks for looking at this issue and for the reply! 🙂 
I've fully refreshed the connection, and it has worked as expected for the last week.
In case of further failure, I'll share the connection state.

@gauth-qobra @rodireich  @ivan-sukhomlyn 

I'm still having the same issues, I have created a new issue to handle this and I had no progress so far: https://github.com/airbytehq/airbyte/issues/70222 

Please add your comment and details there @gauth-qobra
